# Design when (wireframes)

## Never ask

Do **not** ask the human to approve designs, confirm size, confirm track, or “OK to implement?”. Decide and continue.

## Default contract (most UI work)

**Skip `designer`.** Implement from:

- `docs/design-index.json` + `docs/dockyrd-design.html`
- `docs/BRIEFING.md` §9–10 (components + routes)
- `docs/project/patterns/`

Existing artboards cover the 19 dashboard screens; treat them as the visual contract.

## When to run `designer`

| Run designer | Skip |
|--|--|
| Briefing **§17 gaps** (setup wizard, create-flows, team/instance settings, 2FA login step, …) with no artboard yet | Pages already in design-index |
| **L / XL** Feature that changes app shell or IA materially | S / M wiring, API-only, proxy/reconciler internals |
| Human explicitly asks for a wireframe pass | Token polish matching existing screens |

Outputs: `docs/project/issues/<id>/design-direction.md` + `assets/<slug>-wireframe.html` (HTML visual only). Parent continues to **generator** without approval pause.

## Not used in this repo

- Atelier `docs/components/<id>/` wireflow/design packages  
- Studio → WordPress section parity gates

UI exit quality: [dockyard-design-contract](dockyard-design-contract.mdc).
